# CrewSync cron schedule
# ----------------------
# 1. Edit CREWSYNC_DIR below to the absolute path where you cloned this project.
# 2. Make sure the server's timezone is America/New_York (these times are ET):
#       sudo timedatectl set-timezone America/New_York
#    ...or convert the hours to your server's local zone.
# 3. Put your Twilio token in .env (see .env.example). run.sh loads it.
# 4. Install:  crontab crontab.example   (after editing the path)
#
# run.sh loads .env and calls crewsync.py. Logs append to logs/<client>.log.

# --- David's Cozy Cabin: 8am, 6pm, 9pm ET ---
0 8,18,21 * * * cd "/Users/scheck93/Desktop/Cowork Playground/crewsync" && ./run.sh clients/david-cozy-cabin/config.json >> logs/david-cozy-cabin.log 2>&1

# --- One-off example: Conor trial-end reminder on May 29 at 10am ET ---
# Cron has no native "run once" — this fires every May 29. Either remove it
# after it runs, or use `at` instead:
#   echo './run.sh' | at ...   (see README "One-off messages")
# 0 10 29 5 * cd /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/crewsync && ./send_message.sh ... (see README)
